          "analogy": "Think of the settings as the floors of a building and prevention levels as the jobs people do on every floor. You can change a light bulb (primary prevention), fix a leak (secondary), or rebuild a damaged wall (tertiary) on the first floor or the third floor. The floor tells you where you are; the job tells you what you are trying to accomplish."
