            "Limit teaching to 2–3 key points the client needs most, starting with safety.",
            "Use pictures, demonstration, and pill organizers; check numeracy with real tasks such as drawing up a dose.",
            "Ask open-ended teach-back questions: “Tell me how you will take this medicine tomorrow morning.”",
            "Re-teach in a different way if teach-back reveals gaps; never blame the client.",
            "Offer professional interpreters for clients with limited English proficiency; family members are not ideal interpreters.",
            "Provide written materials at a low reading level to reinforce, not replace, verbal teaching."
