          "term": "Primary nursing",
          "def": "A relationship-based model in which one primary nurse (PN) has 24-hour, 7-day authority and responsibility for an assigned group of clients from admission through discharge, assessing, planning, and delivering direct care. Offers high continuity and accountability but requires more RNs."
