          "heading": "How the NCLEX tests this: delivery models and delegation decisions",
          "body": "<p>Expect items that <b>(1) identify the model</b> from a description, <b>(2) choose a model</b> for a staffing situation, <b>(3) ask what to delegate or assign</b> to UAP or LPNs, <b>(4) test accountability</b> (“Who is responsible when…”), and <b>(5) test allocation</b> of a scarce resource. Sample question: <em>“An RN team leader is working with an LPN and a UAP on a medical unit. Which task is most appropriate for the RN to delegate to the UAP?”</em> A. Assessing the skin of a client admitted with a stage 2 pressure injury. B. Assisting a client with stable chronic heart failure to ambulate to the bathroom. C. Teaching a client newly diagnosed with diabetes how to check blood glucose. D. Monitoring a client who returned from a cardiac catheterization 30 minutes ago.</p>",
